ntal pillars for understanding truth - Pathos, Logos, Ethos, and Eros.Logos refers to logical reasoning and argumentation. It is an appeal to rationality, a search for clarity, in pursuit of truth and knowledge to make sense of the world. Logos is part of the Philosophy 101 collection",[]],"900006":["This nail polish has a sheer but buildable medium pastel green base with a glowy blue aurora shimmer.In classical philosophy, this is one of four concepts that serves as fundamental pillars for understanding truth - Pathos, Logos, Ethos, and Eros.Pathos relates to emotions and empathy. It is the recognition that humans are not purely rational beings, and an examination of how our emotions shape our experiences and motivations.Pathos is part of the Philosophy 101 collection",["https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_18_2026_11_58_41_AM.jpg?v=1786831927","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_18_2026_11_57_12_AM.jpg?v=1784772828","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_18_2026_11_58_05_AM.jpg?v=1786831986","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_18_2026_11_59_54_AM.jpg?v=1786831927","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_18_2026_12_01_07_PM.jpg?v=1786831987","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_18_2026_12_02_59_PM.jpg?v=1786831986","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_18_2026_11_59_31_AM.jpg?v=1784772827","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ship_of_theseus-01.jpg?v=1786831927","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_07_2026_2_28_14_PM.jpg?v=1784511845","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ship_of_theseus-03.jpg?v=1786831927","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ship_of_theseus-08.jpg?v=1786831927","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ship_of_theseus-10.jpg?v=1786831986","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_07_2026_2_27_41_PM.jpg?v=1784511845","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ship_of_theseus-06.jpg?v=1786831927","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ship_of_theseus-04.jpg?v=1786831986","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_07_2026_2_39_42_PM.jpg?v=1784511845","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_07_2026_2_27_48_PM.jpg?v=1784511787","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_07_2026_2_29_26_PM.jpg?v=1784511787","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_07_2026_2_42_34_PM.jpg?v=1784511787","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_07_2026_2_30_01_PM.jpg?v=1784511786"]],"900007":[null,["https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/20260726_174509.jpg?v=1786831928","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/20260726_174612.jpg?v=1786831987","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/pp_resize_1.png?v=1789649526","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/20260726_175115_1.jpg?v=1786831986","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/20260726_173250.jpg?v=1786831927","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/pp_resize_2.png?v=1785186663","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/PhotoJul152026_21127PM.jpg?v=1784511845","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/PhotoJul152026_20527PM.jpg?v=1784511845","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/PhotoJul152026_20540PM.jpg?v=1784511787","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/PhotoJul152026_20553PM.jpg?v=1784511786","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/PhotoJul152026_22842PM.jpg?v=1784511788","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/PhotoJul152026_24011PM.jpg?v=1784511787","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/PhotoJul152026_21024PM.jpg?v=1784511845","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/PhotoJul152026_24332PM.jpg?v=1784511787","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ametrine-solipsism7.png?v=1784511789","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ametrine-solipsism3.png?v=1784511787","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ametrine-solipsism4.png?v=1784511788","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ametrine-solipsism5.png?v=1784511845","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ametrine-solipsism6.png?v=1784511787","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ametrine-solipsism1.png?v=1784511845"]],"900008":["This nail polish has a soft minty green base with a shifting aurora holo shimmer that changes from teal, to blue, to gold, and an added holo shimmer. The Ship of Theseus is a famous thought experiment about identity. Imagine a ship belonging to the legendary Greek hero Theseus. Over time, its wooden planks begin to rot, so they are replaced one by one. Eventually, every single original plank has been replaced. The question that is then raised is, is it still the same ship after every plank has been changed out? Most people will generally say yes, it is.But now, suppose that someone collected all of the original parts of the ship that had been replaced over time, and constructed another ship of all of those original parts. Now we have two ships - are they both the Ship of Theseus? Is only one of them the ship? And if so, which one? There aren't really any right or wrong answers to these questions. The experiment serves to help us examine how we think about what makes something itself.My deepest condolences if you just wanted to buy some nail polish and now your head hurts. Ship of Theseus is part of the Philosophy 101 collection",["https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ametrine-sorites4.png?v=1784511786","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ametrine-sorites3.png?v=1784511787","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ametrine-sorites6.png?v=1784511786","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ametrine-sorites7.png?v=1784511845","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ametrine-sorites1.png?v=1784511845","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ametrine-sorites5.png?v=1784511787","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/PhotoJul122026_113023AM.jpg?v=1784511786","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/PhotoJul122026_112048AM.jpg?v=1784511787","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/PhotoJul122026_112058AM.jpg?v=1784511787","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/PhotoJul122026_112925AM.jpg?v=1784511845","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/PhotoJul122026_112937AM.jpg?v=1784511845","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/PhotoJul122026_111707AM.jpg?v=1784511787","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/PhotoJul122026_111637AM.jpg?v=1784511787","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_14_2026_6_04_42_PM.jpg?v=1784772906","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_14_2026_6_03_14_PM.jpg?v=1789649526","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_14_2026_6_03_49_PM.jpg?v=1789649526","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_14_2026_6_03_05_PM.jpg?v=1789649526","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_14_2026_6_05_50_PM.jpg?v=1786831928","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_14_2026_6_06_00_PM.jpg?v=1786831927","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_21_2026_9_11_33_AM.jpg?v=1789649526"]],"900009":["This nail polish is a sparkly denim blue shimmer that shifts from purple, to pink, to red with blue holo magnetic pull. Solipsism is the belief that the only thing that exists is your own conscious mind, that your life, all of the people that we interact with, the world around us, even the entire universe - all of that only exists within your own experience, and is a projection of your own consciousness.Solipsism is part of the Philosophy 101 collection (Please note: This polish has a holo magnetic pigment, after mixing they can sometimes degrade and lose their pull after a couple of years in storage whereas regular magnetic pigments typically do not. I have prototypes with this pigment that I have had for 6+ months with no change so far. They also do not always magnetize quite as crisply as other magnetic pigments. You should still see results that match the swatch photos in comparable lighting.)",["https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_23_2026_4_08_00_PM.jpg?v=1786831926","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_23_2026_4_05_28_PM.jpg?v=1786831986","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_23_2026_4_16_43_PM.jpg?v=1786831928","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_23_2026_4_13_33_PM.jpg?v=1786831927","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_23_2026_4_20_19_PM.jpg?v=1786831987","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_23_2026_4_11_14_PM.jpg?v=1786831926","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/PhotoJul152026_52923PM.jpg?v=1784428926","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/PhotoJul152026_53057PM.jpg?v=1784428926","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/PhotoJul152026_53132PM.jpg?v=1784428926","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/PhotoJul152026_53253PM.jpg?v=1784428926","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/PhotoJul152026_52859PM.jpg?v=1784428927","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ametrine-swampwater4.png?v=1784511787","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ametrine-swampwater5.png?v=1784511789","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ametrine-swampwater6.png?v=1784511787","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ametrine-swampwater7.png?v=1784511787","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ametrine-swampwater1.png?v=1784511788","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/ametrine-swampwater3.png?v=1784511787","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/20260727_231105.jpg?v=1786831987","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/20260727_232050.jpg?v=1786831986","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/pap_resize_sw_1.png?v=1786831986"]],"900010":["This nail polish has an orchid purple base with pink-gold magnetic pull. The Sorites Paradox is sort of a philosophical paradox related to vagueness. It examines how we define terms and use them practically. The classic example is this:A collection of 10,000 grains of sand is a heap of sand, but at which grain of sand did it become a heap? How many grains of sand would we need to remove before it is no longer a heap? The paradox asks if adding one grain of sand doesn't make a heap, when does it become a heap? Similarly, if buying one bottle of nail polish doesn't make it an addiction, at what exact bottle number should I start being concerned? If the line is a blurry one, then theoretically I'm only ever one bottle of polish away from having a perfectly normal hobby. Sorites Paradox is part of the Philosophy 101 collection",["https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Bundle3.jpg?v=1789649526","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_19_2026_16_09_28_56ba9448-db95-46ab-8c1b-f77e87c29e32.jpg?v=1789649526","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_19_2026_16_09_44_6f6eabb3-28d6-4924-9033-e3cc3df9ecf0.jpg?v=1789649526","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_19_2026_16_21_13_c9663884-4d5c-4a9f-afc6-883ed5d0a3d5.jpg?v=1789649526","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/Photo_Jul_19_2026_16_08_59_99f10b99-6088-4933-8023-fc10248bf08e.jpg?v=1789649526","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0772/8168/9785/files/collage_all_launch_polishes_-_1_37440b57-8c14-4658-b75d-c97dccb3a3d7.png?v=1789649526"]],"900011":["This nail polish has a sheer but buildable deep grungy green base with bright blue-purple aurora shimmer.Who doesn't love a good prugly? Swamp Water is named for its inspiration. Swamp Water is available as part of the Bonus Release collection",[]]}